    'eyes-swann-cards-1111': { pri: 1, group: G2, title: 'SWANN\'S READING: Sylvia deals these rows six at a time -- her bar over each door, one key an answer, her table at the deck\'s end (11-11)', pt: 'the eyes lane, the Swann tour seat 11-11 (js/tour.js DS.TOUR: the deck, the store, the bar; deep16/js/swann.js: her table and her booth\'s READ THE CARDS; mode=swann1111) · eyes',
      obj: 'Open Sylvia Swann\'s table and work through six cards — does one key answer each and carry you to the next?',
      url: 'deep16/?cards&fresh=1111',
      look: 'Her table: six cards face down on her cloth, her line, and the owl\'s count of the whole list. TURN THE NEXT CARD (or click a card) opens that card\'s door with her bar across the top -- her face, the deck\'s six as small cards, CARD 1/6 -- and the card up: what should happen, the row\'s own words. Read it, then Enter (or a click on the game) lays the card down and the page is yours to play; H brings the card back. Then one key: 1 works, 2 broken, 3 unclear (2 and 3 open a line for your words at once: Enter keeps them), 4 too hard, 5 too easy, N a note, P pass ("don\'t need to see it": the note "passed", which cuts the row at the fold like any note). Each answer goes on to the next card face down; the arrows walk the deck. The last sends you back to her table, where the cards you answered turn over one by one in your answers\' colours and she has a word for the builders. DEAL SIX MORE for the next six: the most wanted first, a place\'s rows together. SAVE at her table writes your ear file as situations.html\'s Save does -- it is the same store, so the situations page shows every card you answered, marked. Since her table was opened, her booth in Silverton asks THE CUP or READ THE CARDS (BOOTH ON/OFF at her table\'s top right; never in the story). The rows whose doors are off the grid (snoot-mode/, the first game) she leaves to the situations page and says how many. Mark this row on the situations page, or say it in chat.' },
