    // THE BUG FIXES OF 11-10 (the bug fixes seat, on his record of 11-09 and his rulings "3 - fix / 4 - build / 5 - fix"; mode=bugfix1110) -- menus, to be tested by his hands
    'eyes-pocketgear-1110': { pri: 1, group: G2, title: 'The Pocket DM: a weapon taken up in a fight stays on the card, and EQUIP\'s ALT row throws the pack\'s handaxes (11-10)', pt: 'the Pocket DM and the races, the bug fixes seat 11-10 (deep16/js/pocket.js PK.fightKept, PK.packBack, PK.gearOf; js/menu.js the ALT row; deep16/js/battle.js thrownLeft, spendThrow) · eyes',
      obj: 'Buy a scimitar and handaxes, take the blade up mid-fight, throw the axes next — does the blade stay in hand?',
      url: 'deep16/?pocket&fresh=1110bf',
      look: 'Your "Bought Harley a scimitar and it\'s absent on the camp screen, so its unequipped when we enter the fight": buy a weapon at THE MARKET (it waits in the pack), start a fight without putting it on, and take it up in the fight (M, EQUIP: the weapon or the off hand -- the action). After the fight, THE CAMP\'s menu EQUIP shows it worn by that card, and the next fight starts with it in hand; what it put down is in the pack. Then your "thrown weapons from the pack": buy two or three handaxes (or daggers, or spears), and at THE CAMP open EQUIP on a card -- the last row is ALT; its choices are the pack\'s thrown weapons with their count and range. Pick the handaxes: the row reads "Handaxe x3". In the next fight that card has THROW HANDAXE on the ring, 20/60 ft; each throw is one gone from the pack, and the pack after the fight has fewer (no pick-up). "(its own ...)" on the ALT row puts back what it carried.' },
    'eyes-madestatus-1110': { pri: 2, group: G2, title: 'STATUS > FEATURES for a made character: its class\'s features to its level, its oath or path, its style, its feats, ours marked (11-10)', pt: 'the Pocket DM and the races, the bug fixes seat 11-10 (js/menu.js featureLines, classFeatureLines; deep16/js/sheetpdf.js SP.featureList) · eyes',
      obj: 'At the Pocket DM camp, open STATUS on a character you made — are its FEATURES listed, non-SRD ones in blue?',
      url: 'deep16/?pocket&fresh=1110bs',
      look: 'Your note (B), STATUS > FEATURES saying "Nothing written on the sheet." for a made character: at THE CAMP, THE MENU (M), STATUS on one you made (Harley, PELTIE, wut). FEATURES lists its class\'s features up to its level with their words -- Second Wind and Action Surge for a fighter, Lay on Hands with its pool left and Divine Smite for a paladin -- its subclass\'s, the fighting style it fights by (not always Defense or Great Weapon Fighting), its race\'s, and the feats it took; the ones past the SRD (our own oaths and paths, our feats) are in blue, with a key under the list (your "font-color change", 11-10). A gold line is a button you press in a fight. Barley, Aurdin, Vivian and Lymen keep their own sheets\' lines.' },
