      look: 'Your "Breadline is good except it says that it moves and doesn\'t yet" and then "solid, i assume they get their bread and leave": step off the chapel\'s doorway at seven in the morning and watch. Every seven seconds the one at the front walks up to Aldwin\'s door and goes in; the other three each step up a place. A moment later they come back out with a loaf in hand (a crust drawn at the hands) and walk down the street, round the line and round you, to the nearest other door and in at it. Later someone new comes up behind the line. "Mind the line. It moves." Only in the early hours, as the line is.',
